# Native app structure (`app/`)

| Directory | Purpose | Naming |
|---|---|---|
| `screens/{feature}/` | Feature-grouped screens; one folder per feature | PascalCase + `Screen` suffix |
| `components/` | App-wide primitives + cross-cutting components | PascalCase |
| `navigators/` | React Navigation stacks/tabs/types | `*Navigator.tsx` |
| `hooks/` | Cross-cutting reusable hooks | `use*.ts` |
| `services/` | External clients (analytics, sentry, …); NOT API layer | folder per domain |
| `stores/` | Zustand stores (UI state, persisted prefs, session) | `useNameStore.ts` |
| `queries/` | TanStack Query hooks per resource | `useResourceVerb.ts` |
| `lib/` | Pure utilities (api, queryClient, storage, fonts, …) | camelCase |
| `i18n/` | Translations + i18n init | lowercase |
| `theme/` | (deleted — tokens live in `tailwind.config.js`) | — |
| `types/` | Shared TS types | camelCase |
| `config/` | `env.ts` (Zod-validated), runtime config | — |

## Screen grouping pattern

```
screens/
├── example/        # ExampleScreen.tsx, components/, hooks/
├── auth/           # LoginScreen.tsx, SignUpScreen.tsx, …
├── onboarding/     # WelcomeScreen.tsx, PermissionScreen.tsx
├── profile/        # ProfileScreen.tsx, EditProfileScreen.tsx
└── settings/       # SettingsScreen.tsx, …
```

NEVER flat in `screens/`. Each feature directory may contain its own `components/`, `hooks/`, `types.ts` — promote to `app/components/` / `app/hooks/` only when truly shared.

## Data flow

```
Screen → query hook (usePosts) → TanStack Query → service (postsService) → @/lib/api (axios) → backend
Screen → Zustand store → UI / ephemeral state (form drafts, modals, current step)
```

- **Screens orchestrate**, **components render**. Screens own hooks + state; components receive data via props.
- **One hook per domain**: `usePosts`, `useProfile`, `useFavorites`.
- **One service per domain**: `postsService.ts`, `profileService.ts`. Each function = one endpoint, returning a Zod-validated typed result.
- **Never duplicate** server state into Zustand. If you need it in two screens, both call the same query hook.

## Patterns

- Custom hook to extract shared state + handlers logic (e.g., `usePostForm`).
- Shared types in `app/types/{feature}.ts`. Service + screen + tests import from there.
- TanStack Query `queryKey` factory pattern: export `postKeys = { all, list, detail(id) }` so invalidation is consistent.
- Mutations always include `onSuccess` invalidation of the relevant queries.

## Code reuse

- **No copy-paste between screens.** If two screens share state-and-handlers, extract a hook.
- Screen-local components live in `screens/{feature}/components/`. Promote to `app/components/` only when reused across features.
- Generic, business-logic-free UI lives in `app/components/`.

## Required UI states

Every screen must handle: **loading**, **empty**, **error**, **populated**. Use:
- `<LoadingState />` for query.isPending
- `<ErrorState onRetry={…} />` for query.isError
- `<EmptyState />` for empty data
- inline render for populated

## Lists

- `>30 items` → `<ListView />` (FlashList) with `estimatedItemSize`. NEVER `FlatList`.
- Memoize `renderItem` and `keyExtractor` with `useCallback`.
- Avoid inline objects in `renderItem` — pre-compute item-level data.
